<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-DJL year net loss widens in 95/96.</title>
<headline>RTRS-DJL year net loss widens in 95/96.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating			 loss 5.67 vs profit 15.30</p>
<p>    Net				loss 27.67 vs loss 15.79</p>
<p>    Extraordinary	     profit 222.99 vs profit 56.67</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 loss 13.44 vs loss 45.63</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Sales				  490.78 vs 1,726.37</p>
<p>    Other income			  74.12 vs 119.54</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		     loss 15.6 vs loss 8.9</p>
<p>    Tax					1.63 vs 4.67</p>
<p>    Interest				46.04 vs 111.68</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   8.91 vs 32.79</p>
<p>    Minorities		    charge 6.93 vs gain 19.20</p>
<p>NOTE: DJL Ltd is part of the Adelaide Steamship Co Ltd group or companies. The results are reported on a consolidated economic entity basis. DJL said the abnormal loss reflected provision for losses on associated company loans and guarantees and provision for warranty payment. It said extraordinary profit reflected the sale of David Jones Ltd retail operations, which were sold late 1995.  -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
